# Only the frontend is deployed here. The backend needs a long-running process
# and goes to Render, so shipping it to Vercel just slows the upload.
#
# Every pattern is anchored with a leading slash on purpose. Unanchored, `data/`
# also matches `frontend/src/data/` — which is where callRuns.js, plans.js and
# the question bank live — and the build fails on Vercel while still passing
# locally, because Windows had already resolved those imports from disk.
/backend/
/backend-py/
/data/
/node_modules/
/frontend/node_modules/
/frontend/dist/
**/__pycache__/
**/.venv/
*.log
